  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"B. Zix, Delin. &amp; Sculpsi." "Dédiés à son ami Louis Bocherini." Illustrated title page of violino primo part shows figure sitting above in cloud, playing a lyre; figure on lower left holding shield on which is printed: Brevet d'invention, caractères mobiles et planches solides, systême, fonerie et imprimerie de F. Reinhard; and angelic figure with wings with a cornucopia on his left, holding a large medallion with a bas relief identified as I. Gutenberg. The medallion is also supported in part by a cherub, who is also supporting a set of alphabet and musical-symbol blocks. Remaining parts have a label on title page with decorative border surrounding text "9e. Oeuvre de quatuors de Pleyel" followed by a part designation (violino secondo, alto, and basso).</subfield>
    <subfield code="8">01</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Vla and vlc parts labeled as a-vla and b.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"B. Zix, Delin. &amp; Sculpsi." "Dédiés à son ami Louis Bocherini." Illustrated title page of violino primo part shows figure sitting above in cloud, playing a lyre; figure on lower left holding shield on which is printed: Brevet d'invention, caractères mobiles et planches solides, systême, fonerie et imprimerie de F. Reinhard; and angelic figure with wings with a cornucopia on his left, holding a large medallion with a bas relief identified as I. Gutenberg. The medallion is also supported in part by a cherub, who is also supporting a set of alphabet and musical-symbol blocks. Remaining parts have a label on title page with decorative border surrounding text "9e. Oeuvre de quatuors de Pleyel" followed by a part designation (violino secondo, alto, and basso). Printed using Reinhard's stereotype printing process.</subfield>
    <subfield code="3">holdings/199624</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"B. Zix, Delin. &amp; Sculpsi." "Dédiés à son ami Louis Bocherini." Illustrated title page of violino primo part shows figure sitting above in cloud, playing a lyre; figure on lower left holding shield on which is printed: Brevet d'invention, caractères mobiles et planches solides, systême, fonerie et imprimerie de F. Reinhard; and angelic figure with wings with a cornucopia on his left, holding a large medallion with a bas relief identified as I. Gutenberg. The medallion is also supported in part by a cherub, who is also supporting a set of alphabet and musical-symbol blocks. Remaining parts have a label on title page with decorative border surrounding text "9e. Oeuvre de quatuors de Pleyel" followed by a part designation (violino secondo, alto, and basso). Printed using Reinhard's stereotype printing process.</subfield>
